-- title:
--   The n-torsion quotient of a norm-one torus Hopf algebra
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field of characteristic zero, let $c \in K$ be non-zero and not a square, let $n$ be a prime, and fix $\delta$ in an algebraic closure $\overline{K}$ with $\delta^{2} = c$. Let $B_0$ be a commutative $K$-Hopf algebra whose comultiplication is cocommutative, and let $u_0, v_0 \in B_0$ satisfy: $K[u_0,v_0] = B_0$ (the $K$-subalgebra generated by $u_0,v_0$ is the whole of $B_0$), $u_0^{2} - c\,v_0^{2} = 1$, $\Delta u_0 = u_0 \otimes u_0 + c\,(v_0 \otimes v_0)$, $\Delta v_0 = u_0 \otimes v_0 + v_0 \otimes u_0$, and the lifting property that for every $w,z \in \overline{K}$ with $w^{2} - c z^{2} = 1$ there is exactly one $K$-algebra map $g : B_0 \to \overline{K}$ with $g u_0 = w$, $g v_0 = z$. Let $P,Q \in B_0$ satisfy the same quadratic relation $P^{2} - c Q^{2} = 1$ and the same two comultiplication formulas (with $P,Q$ in place of $u_0,v_0$), together with $\varepsilon P = 1$, $\varepsilon Q = 0$, and the $n$-th power condition $f P \pm f Q\,\delta = (f u_0 \pm f v_0\,\delta)^{n}$ for every $K$-algebra map $f : B_0 \to \overline{K}$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a commutative ring $A$ with a cocommutative $K$-Hopf algebra structure and elements $u',v' \in A$ generating $A$ over $K$, satisfying $u'^{2} - c\,v'^{2} = 1$ and the same two comultiplication formulas, such that $(f u' + f v'\,\delta)^{n} = 1$ for every $K$-algebra map $f : A \to \overline{K}$, and such that every pair $(w,z)$ in $\overline{K}$ with $w^{2} - c z^{2} = 1$ and $(w + z\delta)^{n} = 1$ is realised by a unique $K$-algebra map $f : A \to \overline{K}$ with $f u' = w$, $f v' = z$.
--
--   In geometric terms, $B_0$ is the coordinate ring of the norm-one torus $T = \mathrm{Res}^{(1)}_{K(\sqrt{c})/K}\mathbb{G}_m$, the pair $(P,Q)$ presents the $n$-th power map on $T$, and the theorem produces the coordinate ring of the finite group scheme $T[n]$, characterised by its $\overline{K}$-points. It feeds the construction of the $n$-torsion of such tori used downstream in [`HopfAlgebra.exists_cocomm_adjoin_nTorsion_quotient_of_adjoin_normOneTorus`](thm.html#HopfAlgebra.exists_cocomm_adjoin_nTorsion_quotient_of_adjoin_normOneTorus).
